#{[{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186198380 :knowledge-point/canonical-example {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186198022 :knowledge-point/_canonical-example [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "f322cca7-7530-50bf-b262-89faa81f5906" :knowledge-point/title "Evaluating Flux Through a Surface"}] :question/id #uuid "0364a11f-e567-517e-acf2-471708dbdc0a" :question/math-academy-id "e-12358" :question/problem "Evaluate the surface integral\n\n$$\n\\iint\\limits_S \\left\\langle z, \\: x, \\: y \\right\\rangle \\cdot \\textrm{d}\\mathbf{S}\n$$\n\nwhere the parametric surface $S$ is defined by the equations\n\n$$\n\\mathbf{r}(u,v) = \\left\\langle 1+2u+v, \\: u+v, \\: u-v \\right\\rangle\n$$\n\nfor $0 \\leq u \\leq 2$ and $0 \\leq v \\leq 1.$" :question/worked-solution "For a surface $S$ with parametrization $\\mathbf{r}(u,v)$ for $(u,v) \\in D,$ the flux of a vector field $\\mathbf{F}$ over $S$ is given by\n\n$$\n\\iint\\limits_S \\mathbf{F} \\cdot \\textrm{d}\\mathbf{S}\n=\n\\iint\\limits_S \\mathbf{F} \\cdot \\mathbf{n} \\,\\textrm{d}S\n=\n\\iint\\limits_D \\mathbf{F}(\\mathbf{r}(u,v)) \\cdot (\\mathbf{r}'_u \\times \\mathbf{r}'_v) \\,\\textrm{d}A.\n$$\n\nWe first compute the tangent vectors to the grid curves:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{r}_{u}^{′} & =⟨\\frac{∂x}{∂u},\\,\\frac{∂y}{∂u},\\,\\frac{∂z}{∂u}⟩ \\\\  & =⟨\\frac{∂}{∂u}(1+2u+v),\\,\\frac{∂}{∂u}(u+v),\\,\\frac{∂}{∂u}(u-v)⟩ \\\\  & =⟨2,\\,1,\\,1⟩ \\\\ {r}_{v}^{′} & =⟨\\frac{∂x}{∂v},\\,\\frac{∂y}{∂v},\\,\\frac{∂z}{∂v}⟩ \\\\  & =⟨\\frac{∂}{∂v}(1+2u+v),\\,\\frac{∂}{∂v}(u+v),\\,\\frac{∂}{∂v}(u-v)⟩ \\\\  & =⟨1,\\,1,\\,-1⟩\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, the fundamental vector product is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{r}_{u}^{′}\\times {r}_{v}^{′} & =|\\begin{aligned}i & j & k \\\\ 2 & 1 & 1 \\\\ 1 & 1 & -1\\end{aligned}| \\\\  & =⟨|\\begin{aligned}1 & 1 \\\\ 1 & -1\\end{aligned}|,-|\\begin{aligned}2 & 1 \\\\ 1 & -1\\end{aligned}|,|\\begin{aligned}2 & 1 \\\\ 1 & 1\\end{aligned}|⟩ \\\\  & =⟨-2,\\,3,\\,1⟩.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNext, we substitute the coordinate expressions of $\\mathbf{r}(u,v)$ into $\\mathbf{F}(x,y,z){:}$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}F(r(u,v)) & ={⟨z,\\,x,\\,y⟩|}_{x=1+2u+v\\,y=u+v\\,z=u-v} \\\\  & =⟨u-v,\\,1+2u+v,\\,u+v⟩\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThen, we calculate the dot product of $\\mathbf{F}$ and $\\mathbf{r}'_u \\times \\mathbf{r}'_v{:}$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}F(r(u,v))\\cdot ({r}_{u}^{′}\\times {r}_{v}^{′}) & =⟨u-v,\\,1+2u+v,\\,u+v⟩\\cdot ⟨-2,\\,3,\\,1⟩ \\\\  & =(u-v)\\cdot (-2)+(1+2u+v)\\cdot 3+(u+v)\\cdot 1 \\\\  & =-2u+2v+3+6u+3v+u+v \\\\  & =5u+6v+3\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the surface integral evaluates to\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{∬}_{S}⟨z,\\,x,\\,y⟩\\cdot \\text{d}S & ={∬}_{D}F(r(u,v))\\cdot ({r}_{u}^{′}\\times {r}_{v}^{′})\\,\\text{d}A \\\\  & ={∬}_{D}(5u+6v+3)\\,\\text{d}A \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{2}{\\int }_{0}^{1}(5u+6v+3)\\,\\text{d}v\\,\\text{d}u \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{2}[5uv+3{v}^{2}+3v]_{v=0}^{v=1}\\,\\text{d}u \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{2}(5u+6)\\,\\text{d}u \\\\  & ={[\\frac{5}{2}{u}^{2}+6u]}_{0}^{2} \\\\  & =10+12 \\\\  & =22.\\end{aligned}\n$$"} :knowledge-point/id #uuid "f322cca7-7530-50bf-b262-89faa81f5906" :knowledge-point/question-generator {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186531837 :question-generator/id #uuid "f02c8d68-61bb-596d-b8ac-ee422698f15e" :question-generator/script "generate/scratch/17592186198380.py"} :knowledge-point/questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186198586 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "f322cca7-7530-50bf-b262-89faa81f5906" :knowledge-point/title "Evaluating Flux Through a Surface"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "0183618f-3362-5caf-80a5-a35db56f915e" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "10" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186275488} {:answer/id #uuid "0e6cd527-baf3-578b-b158-575236e38ff7" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186275598} {:answer/id #uuid "12c49c9b-d152-58b2-80d7-d4d05c4ba56d" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "8" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186275647} {:answer/id #uuid "5e5a323e-80aa-5ee5-8b05-f4d65a56b56b" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "4" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186276320} {:answer/id #uuid "f8a62071-81ac-50dc-be9e-62be7ce3c24d" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "6" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186277652}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "f8a62071-81ac-50dc-be9e-62be7ce3c24d" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "6" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186277652} :answer-field/id #uuid "180f5e20-4b61-50e3-abd0-cd720a92e5b8" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186277769}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045486 :db/ident :question.difficulty/hard} :question/id #uuid "69fe42a1-24c6-5f53-90f3-883e2fa5e193" :question/math-academy-id "q-160845" :question/problem "Evaluate the surface integral\n\n$$\n{∬}_{S}⟨3x+y+z,\\,\\frac{y}{2}-2,\\,-3x-z⟩\\cdot \\text{d}S\n$$\n\nwhere the parametric surface $S$ is defined by the equations\n\n$$\nr(u,v)=⟨u-1,\\,2v,\\,2-3u-2v⟩\n$$\n\nfor $-1\\le u\\le 1$ and $0\\le v\\le 3.$" :question/worked-solution "For a surface $S$ with parametrization $r(u,v)$ for $(u,v)\\in D,$ the flux of a vector field $F$ over $S$ is given by\n\n$$\n{∬}_{S}F\\cdot \\text{d}S={∬}_{S}F\\cdot n\\,\\text{d}S={∬}_{D}F(r(u,v))\\cdot ({r}_{u}^{′}\\times {r}_{v}^{′})\\,\\text{d}A.\n$$\n\nWe first compute the tangent vectors to the grid curves:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{r}_{u}^{′} & =⟨\\frac{∂x}{∂u},\\,\\frac{∂y}{∂u},\\,\\frac{∂z}{∂u}⟩ \\\\  & =⟨\\frac{∂}{∂u}(u-1),\\,\\frac{∂}{∂u}(2v),\\,\\frac{∂}{∂u}(2-3u-2v)⟩ \\\\  & =⟨1,\\,0,\\,-3⟩ \\\\ {r}_{v}^{′} & =⟨\\frac{∂x}{∂v},\\,\\frac{∂y}{∂v},\\,\\frac{∂z}{∂v}⟩ \\\\  & =⟨\\frac{∂}{∂v}(u-1),\\,\\frac{∂}{∂v}(2v),\\,\\frac{∂}{∂v}(2-3u-2v)⟩ \\\\  & =⟨0,\\,2,\\,-2⟩\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, the fundamental vector product is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{r}_{u}^{′}\\times {r}_{v}^{′} & =|\\begin{aligned}i & j & k \\\\ 1 & 0 & -3 \\\\ 0 & 2 & -2\\end{aligned}| \\\\  & =⟨|\\begin{aligned}0 & -3 \\\\ 2 & -2\\end{aligned}|,-|\\begin{aligned}1 & -3 \\\\ 0 & -2\\end{aligned}|,|\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 2\\end{aligned}|⟩ \\\\  & =⟨6,\\,2,\\,2⟩.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNext, we substitute the coordinate expressions of $r(u,v)$ into $F(x,y,z):$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}F(r(u,v)) & ={⟨3x+y+z,\\,\\frac{y}{2}-2,\\,-3x-z⟩|}_{x=u-1\\,y=2v\\,z=2-3u-2v} \\\\  & =⟨3(u-1)+(2v)+(2-3u-2v),\\,\\frac{2v}{2}-2,\\,-3(u-1)-(2-3u-2v)⟩ \\\\  & =⟨-1,\\,v-2,\\,2v+1⟩\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, we calculate the dot product of $F$ and ${r}_{u}^{′}\\times {r}_{v}^{′}:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}F(r(u,v))\\cdot ({r}_{u}^{′}\\times {r}_{v}^{′}) & =⟨-1,\\,v-2,\\,2v+1⟩\\cdot ⟨6,\\,2,\\,2⟩ \\\\  & =(-1)\\cdot 6+(v-2)\\cdot 2+(2v+1)\\cdot 2 \\\\  & =-6+2v-4+4v+2 \\\\  & =6v-8.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the surface integral evaluates to\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{∬}_{S}⟨3x+y+z,\\,\\frac{y}{2}-2,\\,-3x-z⟩\\cdot \\text{d}S & ={∬}_{D}F(r(u,v))\\cdot ({r}_{u}^{′}\\times {r}_{v}^{′})\\,\\text{d}A \\\\  & ={∬}_{D}(6v-8)\\,\\text{d}A \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{3}{\\int }_{-1}^{1}(6v-8)\\,\\text{d}u\\text{d}v \\\\  & ={\\int }_{-1}^{1}\\,\\text{d}u\\cdot {\\int }_{0}^{3}(6v-8)\\,\\text{d}v \\\\  & =[u]_{-1}^{1}\\cdot [3{v}^{2}-8v]_{0}^{3} \\\\  & =2\\cdot 3 \\\\  & =6.\\end{aligned}\n$$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186198592 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "f322cca7-7530-50bf-b262-89faa81f5906" :knowledge-point/title "Evaluating Flux Through a Surface"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "11be498b-977a-5f13-82a0-b8754dc5bd8e" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "48" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186275636} {:answer/id #uuid "8b18291e-b1ba-55db-80ed-c83639075677" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "18" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186276737} {:answer/id #uuid "bc028827-be53-5841-a899-754876ec3402" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "36" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186277150} {:answer/id #uuid "d4a0b90a-2bd6-5552-afc1-f83bdcf172c8" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "72" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186277350} {:answer/id #uuid "eb4662bc-b4e4-5fee-98bc-64e89c915aa4" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "24" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186277533}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "8b18291e-b1ba-55db-80ed-c83639075677" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "18" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186276737} :answer-field/id #uuid "42073408-3ed9-5a4e-b4da-76268342b625" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186277827}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "e6b5a3a2-513f-5721-bf54-260cfc8a8f5a" :question/math-academy-id "q-160886" :question/problem "Evaluate the surface integral\n\n$$\n{∬}_{S}⟨2x,\\,\\frac{xz}{3}-2y,\\,2z⟩\\cdot \\text{d}S\n$$\n\nwhere the parametric surface $S$ is defined by\n\n$$\nr(u,v)=⟨2u-1,\\,uv,\\,3v⟩\n$$\n\nover the domain $D={(u,v)\\,:\\,0\\le u\\le 1,\\,-1\\le v\\le 2}.$\n\n*Hint: You can use the fact that ${r}_{u}^{′}\\times {r}_{v}^{′}=⟨3v,\\,-6,\\,2u⟩.$*" :question/worked-solution "For a surface $S$ with parametrization $r(u,v)$ for $(u,v)\\in D,$ the flux of a vector field $F$ over $S$ is given by\n\n$$\n{∬}_{S}F\\cdot \\text{d}S={∬}_{S}F\\cdot n\\,\\text{d}S={∬}_{D}F(r(u,v))\\cdot ({r}_{u}^{′}\\times {r}_{v}^{′})\\,\\text{d}A.\n$$\n\nWe're given that the fundamental vector product for our surface is\n\n$$\n{r}_{u}^{′}\\times {r}_{v}^{′}=⟨3v,\\,-6,\\,2u⟩.\n$$\n\nNext, we substitute the coordinate expressions of $r(u,v)$ into $F(x,y,z):$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}F(r(u,v)) & ={⟨2x,\\,\\frac{xz}{3}-2y,\\,2z⟩|}_{x=2u-1\\,y=uv\\,z=3v} \\\\  & =⟨2(2u-1),\\,\\frac{(2u-1)(3v)}{3}-2uv,\\,2(3v)⟩ \\\\  & =⟨4u-2,\\,-v,\\,6v⟩\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThen, we calculate the dot product of $F$ and ${r}_{u}^{′}\\times {r}_{v}^{′}:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}F(r(u,v))\\cdot ({r}_{u}^{′}\\times {r}_{v}^{′}) & =⟨4u-2,\\,-v,\\,6v⟩\\cdot ⟨3v,\\,-6,\\,2u⟩ \\\\  & =(4u-2)\\cdot 3v+(-v)\\cdot (-6)+6v\\cdot 2u \\\\  & =12uv-6v+6v+12uv \\\\  & =24uv.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the surface integral evaluates to\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{∬}_{S}⟨2x,\\,\\frac{xz}{3}-2y,\\,2z⟩\\cdot \\text{d}S & ={∬}_{D}F(r(u,v))\\cdot ({r}_{u}^{′}\\times {r}_{v}^{′})\\,\\text{d}A \\\\  & ={∬}_{D}24uv\\,\\text{d}A \\\\  & ={\\int }_{-1}^{2}{\\int }_{0}^{1}24uv\\,\\text{d}u\\text{d}v \\\\  & ={\\int }_{-1}^{2}[12{u}^{2}v]_{0}^{1}\\,\\text{d}v \\\\  & ={\\int }_{-1}^{2}12v\\,\\text{d}v \\\\  & =[6{v}^{2}]_{-1}^{2} \\\\  & =6({2}^{2}-(-1)^{2}) \\\\  & =18.\\end{aligned}\n$$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186278448 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "f322cca7-7530-50bf-b262-89faa81f5906" :knowledge-point/title "Evaluating Flux Through a Surface"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "4eb1ebbc-1b66-59c6-bc4c-36473d96ba4c" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-\\frac{1}{3}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186276175} {:answer/id #uuid "85d8c729-3067-5308-8ef9-00bf4d3de7e8" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186276678} {:answer/id #uuid "89edd3d9-c58a-5b81-ba4b-f7481df906e2" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-\\frac{5}{6}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186276723} {:answer/id #uuid "a74d2bae-d261-5258-af7b-a10ec79ffeaa" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186276985} {:answer/id #uuid "dc49e905-67e7-5a8f-9ad4-5d61bb70fa97" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "4" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186277407}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "4eb1ebbc-1b66-59c6-bc4c-36473d96ba4c" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-\\frac{1}{3}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186276175} :answer-field/id #uuid "8068e66d-fe19-5730-b61d-8b3c05169a3b" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186277949}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "24885575-8fa2-5424-9a08-3593cc23273c" :question/math-academy-id "q-161260" :question/problem "Evaluate the surface integral\n\n$$\n{∬}_{S}⟨y+z,\\,x+z,\\,1⟩\\cdot \\text{d}S\n$$\n\nwhere the parametric surface $S$ is defined by\n\n$$\nr(u,v)=⟨u-v,\\,2,\\,{v}^{2}⟩\n$$\n\nover the domain $D={(u,v)\\,:\\,0\\le u\\le 1,\\,0\\le v\\le 1}.$\n\n*Hint: You can use the fact that ${r}_{u}^{′}\\times {r}_{v}^{′}=⟨0,\\,-2v,\\,0⟩.$*" :question/worked-solution "For a surface $S$ with parametrization $r(u,v)$ for $(u,v)\\in D,$ the flux of a vector field $F$ over $S$ is given by\n\n$$\n{∬}_{S}F\\cdot \\text{d}S={∬}_{S}F\\cdot n\\,\\text{d}S={∬}_{D}F(r(u,v))\\cdot ({r}_{u}^{′}\\times {r}_{v}^{′})\\,\\text{d}A.\n$$\n\nWe're given that the fundamental vector product for our surface is\n\n$$\n{r}_{u}^{′}\\times {r}_{v}^{′}=⟨0,\\,-2v,\\,0⟩.\n$$\n\nNext, we substitute the coordinate expressions of $r(u,v)$ into $F(x,y,z):$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}F(r(u,v)) & ={⟨y+z,\\,x+z,\\,1⟩|}_{x=u-v\\,y=2\\,z={v}^{2}} \\\\  & =⟨2+{v}^{2},\\,u-v+{v}^{2},\\,1⟩\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThen, we calculate the dot product of $F$ and ${r}_{u}^{′}\\times {r}_{v}^{′}:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}F(r(u,v))\\cdot ({r}_{u}^{′}\\times {r}_{v}^{′}) & =⟨2+{v}^{2},\\,u-v+{v}^{2},\\,1⟩\\cdot ⟨0,\\,-2v,\\,0⟩ \\\\  & =(2+{v}^{2})\\cdot 0+(u-v+{v}^{2})\\cdot (-2v)+1\\cdot 0 \\\\  & =-2uv+2{v}^{2}-2{v}^{3}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the surface integral evaluates to\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{∬}_{S}⟨y+z,\\,x+z,\\,1⟩\\cdot \\text{d}S & ={∬}_{D}F(r(u,v))\\cdot ({r}_{u}^{′}\\times {r}_{v}^{′})\\,\\text{d}A \\\\  & ={∬}_{D}(-2uv+2{v}^{2}-2{v}^{3})\\,\\text{d}A \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{1}{\\int }_{0}^{1}(-2uv+2{v}^{2}-2{v}^{3})\\,\\text{d}u\\,\\text{d}v \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{1}[-{u}^{2}v+2u{v}^{2}-2u{v}^{3}]_{u=0}^{u=1}\\,\\text{d}v \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{1}(-v+2{v}^{2}-2{v}^{3})\\text{d}v \\\\  & ={[-\\frac{1}{2}{v}^{2}+\\frac{2}{3}{v}^{3}-\\frac{1}{2}{v}^{4}]}_{0}^{1} \\\\  & =-\\frac{1}{2}+\\frac{2}{3}-\\frac{1}{2} \\\\  & =-\\frac{1}{3}.\\end{aligned}\n$$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186278449 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "f322cca7-7530-50bf-b262-89faa81f5906" :knowledge-point/title "Evaluating Flux Through a Surface"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "44b20462-99c7-5dec-bd31-d1e7bfd2d3e6" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "11" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186276083} {:answer/id #uuid "47ec0a42-a449-5ef7-9620-57343f2509fc" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{9}{4}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186276115} {:answer/id #uuid "9a3c185d-7cc5-59b9-a34a-f883b39b5057" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "5" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186276862} {:answer/id #uuid "bb763c3b-1014-5b4d-aa64-f7778d6ff1dd" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{5}{3}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186277143} {:answer/id #uuid "ec28bfe5-83c3-5b4b-bd6b-4c685f49f886" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "8" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186277548}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "ec28bfe5-83c3-5b4b-bd6b-4c685f49f886" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "8" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186277548} :answer-field/id #uuid "8345f144-9030-5837-991d-e3b6514dd5e7" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186277957}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "627dbfaa-1fc7-5620-9101-9c85744bbe99" :question/math-academy-id "q-161262" :question/problem "Evaluate the surface integral\n\n$$\n{∬}_{S}⟨{x}^{2},\\,x+y,\\,z⟩\\cdot \\text{d}S\n$$\n\nwhere the parametric surface $S$ is defined by\n\n$$\nr(u,v)=⟨3u{v}^{2},\\,u-v,\\,2⟩\n$$\n\nover the domain $D={(u,v)\\,:\\,-2\\le u\\le 0,\\,0\\le v\\le 1}.$\n\n*Hint: You can use the fact that ${r}_{u}^{′}\\times {r}_{v}^{′}=⟨0,\\,0,\\,-6uv-3{v}^{2}⟩.$*" :question/worked-solution "For a surface $S$ with parametrization $r(u,v)$ for $(u,v)\\in D,$ the flux of a vector field $F$ over $S$ is given by\n\n$$\n{∬}_{S}F\\cdot \\text{d}S={∬}_{S}F\\cdot n\\,\\text{d}S={∬}_{D}F(r(u,v))\\cdot ({r}_{u}^{′}\\times {r}_{v}^{′})\\,\\text{d}A.\n$$\n\nWe're given that the fundamental vector product for our surface is\n\n$$\n{r}_{u}^{′}\\times {r}_{v}^{′}=⟨0,\\,0,\\,-6uv-3{v}^{2}⟩.\n$$\n\nNext, we substitute the coordinate expressions of $r(u,v)$ into $F(x,y,z):$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}F(r(u,v)) & ={⟨{x}^{2},\\,x+y,\\,z⟩|}_{x=3u{v}^{2}\\,y=u-v\\,z=2} \\\\  & =⟨{(3u{v}^{2})}^{2},\\,3u{v}^{2}+u-v,\\,2⟩ \\\\  & =⟨9{u}^{2}{v}^{4},\\,3u{v}^{2}+u-v,\\,2⟩\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThen, we calculate the dot product of $F$ and ${r}_{u}^{′}\\times {r}_{v}^{′}:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}F(r(u,v))\\cdot ({r}_{u}^{′}\\times {r}_{v}^{′}) & =⟨9{u}^{2}{v}^{4},\\,3u{v}^{2}+u-v,\\,2⟩\\cdot ⟨0,\\,0,\\,-6uv-3{v}^{2}⟩ \\\\  & =9{u}^{2}{v}^{4}\\cdot 0+(3u{v}^{2}+u-v)\\cdot 0+2\\cdot (-6uv-3{v}^{2}) \\\\  & =-6(2uv+{v}^{2})\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the surface integral evaluates to\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{∬}_{S}⟨{x}^{2},\\,x+y,\\,z⟩\\cdot \\text{d}S & ={∬}_{D}F(r(u,v))\\cdot ({r}_{u}^{′}\\times {r}_{v}^{′})\\,\\text{d}A \\\\  & ={∬}_{D}-6(2uv+{v}^{2})\\,\\text{d}A \\\\  & =-6{\\int }_{-2}^{0}{\\int }_{0}^{1}(2uv+{v}^{2})\\,\\text{d}v\\,\\text{d}u \\\\  & =-6{\\int }_{-2}^{0}{[u{v}^{2}+\\frac{1}{3}{v}^{3}]}_{v=0}^{v=1}\\,\\text{d}u \\\\  & =-6{\\int }_{-2}^{0}(u+\\frac{1}{3})\\text{d}u \\\\  & =-6{[\\frac{1}{2}{u}^{2}+\\frac{1}{3}u]}_{-2}^{0} \\\\  & =-6(-2+\\frac{2}{3}) \\\\  & =8.\\end{aligned}\n$$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186278450 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "f322cca7-7530-50bf-b262-89faa81f5906" :knowledge-point/title "Evaluating Flux Through a Surface"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "23825e40-ec53-5f67-9638-35d121d51307" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "4" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186275793} {:answer/id #uuid "5ec69f15-fbed-5296-9952-1dc103047426" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-3" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186276325} {:answer/id #uuid "98e6e4b9-4435-58e2-9d7a-b732cdd0ce08" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-\\frac{1}{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186276849} {:answer/id #uuid "d47ba56f-6b65-598d-b6f5-90728d0382b8" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{5}{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186277348} {:answer/id #uuid "ebed3c1d-caab-55c6-88ae-97fc928a3dae" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186277545}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "5ec69f15-fbed-5296-9952-1dc103047426" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-3" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186276325} :answer-field/id #uuid "20c0bba0-07fc-5c71-ba73-fcc312a83f3b" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186277781}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045486 :db/ident :question.difficulty/hard} :question/id #uuid "c5de597f-04b0-56f5-aa9e-d79ce26e7706" :question/math-academy-id "q-161263" :question/problem "Evaluate the surface integral\n\n$$\n{∬}_{S}⟨3,\\,z,\\,y⟩\\cdot \\text{d}S\n$$\n\nwhere the parametric surface $S$ is defined by the equations\n\n$$\nr(u,v)=⟨{u}^{2},\\,v,\\,uv⟩\n$$\n\nfor $-1\\le u\\le 1$ and $0\\le v\\le 1.$" :question/worked-solution "For a surface $S$ with parametrization $r(u,v)$ for $(u,v)\\in D,$ the flux of a vector field $F$ over $S$ is given by\n\n$$\n{∬}_{S}F\\cdot \\text{d}S={∬}_{S}F\\cdot n\\,\\text{d}S={∬}_{D}F(r(u,v))\\cdot ({r}_{u}^{′}\\times {r}_{v}^{′})\\,\\text{d}A.\n$$\n\nWe first compute the tangent vectors to the grid curves:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{r}_{u}^{′} & =⟨\\frac{∂x}{∂u},\\,\\frac{∂y}{∂u},\\,\\frac{∂z}{∂u}⟩ \\\\  & =⟨\\frac{∂}{∂u}({u}^{2}),\\,\\frac{∂}{∂u}(v),\\,\\frac{∂}{∂u}(uv)⟩ \\\\  & =⟨2u,\\,0,\\,v⟩ \\\\ {r}_{v}^{′} & =⟨\\frac{∂x}{∂v},\\,\\frac{∂y}{∂v},\\,\\frac{∂z}{∂v}⟩ \\\\  & =⟨\\frac{∂}{∂v}({u}^{2}),\\,\\frac{∂}{∂v}(v),\\,\\frac{∂}{∂v}(uv)⟩ \\\\  & =⟨0,\\,1,\\,u⟩\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, the fundamental vector product is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{r}_{u}^{′}\\times {r}_{v}^{′} & =|\\begin{aligned}i & j & k \\\\ 2u & 0 & v \\\\ 0 & 1 & u\\end{aligned}| \\\\  & =⟨|\\begin{aligned}0 & v \\\\ 1 & 0\\end{aligned}|,-|\\begin{aligned}2u & v \\\\ 0 & u\\end{aligned}|,|\\begin{aligned}2u & 0 \\\\ 0 & 1\\end{aligned}|⟩ \\\\  & =⟨-v,\\,-2{u}^{2},\\,2u⟩.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNext, we substitute the coordinate expressions of $r(u,v)$ into $F(x,y,z):$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}F(r(u,v)) & ={⟨3,\\,z,\\,y⟩|}_{x={u}^{2}\\,y=v\\,z=uv} \\\\  & =⟨3,\\,uv,\\,v⟩\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, we calculate the dot product of $F$ and ${r}_{u}^{′}\\times {r}_{v}^{′}:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}F(r(u,v))\\cdot ({r}_{u}^{′}\\times {r}_{v}^{′}) & =⟨3,\\,uv,\\,v⟩\\cdot ⟨-v,\\,-2{u}^{2},\\,2u⟩ \\\\  & =3\\cdot (-v)+uv\\cdot (-2{u}^{2})+v\\cdot 2u \\\\  & =-3v-2{u}^{3}v+2uv\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the surface integral evaluates to\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{∬}_{S}⟨3,\\,z,\\,y⟩\\cdot \\text{d}S & ={∬}_{D}F(r(u,v))\\cdot ({r}_{u}^{′}\\times {r}_{v}^{′})\\,\\text{d}A \\\\  & ={∬}_{D}(-3v-2{u}^{3}v+2uv)\\,\\text{d}A \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{1}{\\int }_{-1}^{1}(-3v-2{u}^{3}v+2uv)\\,\\text{d}u\\,\\text{d}v \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{1}{[-3uv-\\frac{1}{2}{u}^{4}v+{u}^{2}v]}_{u=-1}^{u=1}\\,\\text{d}v \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{1}(-6v)\\text{d}v \\\\  & =[-3{v}^{2}]_{0}^{1} \\\\  & =-3.\\end{aligned}\n$$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186278455 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "f322cca7-7530-50bf-b262-89faa81f5906" :knowledge-point/title "Evaluating Flux Through a Surface"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "4087a83f-b6d4-59eb-ad43-5778e62db807" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186276039} {:answer/id #uuid "4cf11252-5492-5171-bafa-fea2eb4849ac" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-4" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186276157} {:answer/id #uuid "9a0daa63-b87d-58b0-ad93-81d0749be7b6" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{1}{3}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186276857} {:answer/id #uuid "bb812a7c-457e-5b53-bb9a-157b69c0ee22" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-\\frac{4}{3}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186277146} {:answer/id #uuid "dc487f46-d4f7-596b-b4d5-ade4f4727666" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186277406}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "4cf11252-5492-5171-bafa-fea2eb4849ac" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-4" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186276157} :answer-field/id #uuid "09628fb2-5798-5e67-a99b-89a6c4a88382" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186277743}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045486 :db/ident :question.difficulty/hard} :question/id #uuid "75e371a5-e04a-5fb9-938c-f538e06e2f93" :question/math-academy-id "q-161273" :question/problem "Evaluate the surface integral\n\n$$\n{∬}_{S}⟨x,\\,0,\\,y⟩\\cdot \\text{d}S\n$$\n\nwhere the parametric surface $S$ is defined by the equations\n\n$$\nr(u,v)=⟨u-v,\\,v-u,\\,-2uv⟩\n$$\n\nfor $0\\le u\\le 1$ and $0\\le v\\le 2.$" :question/worked-solution "For a surface $S$ with parametrization $r(u,v)$ for $(u,v)\\in D,$ the flux of a vector field $F$ over $S$ is given by\n\n$$\n{∬}_{S}F\\cdot \\text{d}S={∬}_{S}F\\cdot n\\,\\text{d}S={∬}_{D}F(r(u,v))\\cdot ({r}_{u}^{′}\\times {r}_{v}^{′})\\,\\text{d}A.\n$$\n\nWe first compute the tangent vectors to the grid curves:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{r}_{u}^{′} & =⟨\\frac{∂x}{∂u},\\,\\frac{∂y}{∂u},\\,\\frac{∂z}{∂u}⟩ \\\\  & =⟨\\frac{∂}{∂u}(u-v),\\,\\frac{∂}{∂u}(v-u),\\,\\frac{∂}{∂u}(-2uv)⟩ \\\\  & =⟨1,\\,-1,\\,-2v⟩ \\\\ {r}_{v}^{′} & =⟨\\frac{∂x}{∂v},\\,\\frac{∂y}{∂v},\\,\\frac{∂z}{∂v}⟩ \\\\  & =⟨\\frac{∂}{∂v}(u-v),\\,\\frac{∂}{∂v}(v-u),\\,\\frac{∂}{∂v}(-2uv)⟩ \\\\  & =⟨-1,\\,1,\\,-2u⟩\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, the fundamental vector product is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{r}_{u}^{′}\\times {r}_{v}^{′} & =|\\begin{aligned}i & j & k \\\\ 1 & -1 & -2v \\\\ -1 & 1 & -2u\\end{aligned}| \\\\  & =⟨|\\begin{aligned}-1 & -2v \\\\ 1 & -2u\\end{aligned}|,-|\\begin{aligned}1 & -2v \\\\ -1 & -2u\\end{aligned}|,|\\begin{aligned}1 & -1 \\\\ -1 & 1\\end{aligned}|⟩ \\\\  & =⟨2u+2v,\\,2u+2v,\\,0⟩.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNext, we substitute the coordinate expressions of $r(u,v)$ into $F(x,y,z):$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}F(r(u,v)) & ={⟨x,\\,0,\\,y⟩|}_{x=u-v\\,y=v-u\\,z=-2uv} \\\\  & =⟨u-v,\\,0,\\,v-u⟩\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, we calculate the dot product of $F$ and ${r}_{u}^{′}\\times {r}_{v}^{′}:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}F(r(u,v))\\cdot ({r}_{u}^{′}\\times {r}_{v}^{′}) & =⟨u-v,\\,0,\\,v-u⟩\\cdot ⟨2u+2v,\\,2u+2v,\\,0⟩ \\\\  & =(u-v)\\cdot (2u+2v)+0\\cdot (2u+2v)+(v-u)\\cdot 0 \\\\  & =2({u}^{2}-{v}^{2})\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the surface integral evaluates to\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{∬}_{S}⟨x,\\,0,\\,y⟩\\cdot \\text{d}S & ={∬}_{D}F(r(u,v))\\cdot ({r}_{u}^{′}\\times {r}_{v}^{′})\\,\\text{d}A \\\\  & ={∬}_{D}2({u}^{2}-{v}^{2})\\,\\text{d}A \\\\  & =2{\\int }_{0}^{2}{\\int }_{0}^{1}({u}^{2}-{v}^{2})\\,\\text{d}u\\,\\text{d}v \\\\  & =2{\\int }_{0}^{2}{[\\frac{1}{3}{u}^{3}-u{v}^{2}]}_{u=0}^{u=1}\\,\\text{d}v \\\\  & =2{\\int }_{0}^{2}(\\frac{1}{3}-{v}^{2})\\text{d}v \\\\  & =2{[\\frac{1}{3}v-\\frac{1}{3}{v}^{3}]}_{0}^{2} \\\\  & =2(\\frac{2}{3}-\\frac{8}{3}) \\\\  & =-4.\\end{aligned}\n$$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186278459 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "f322cca7-7530-50bf-b262-89faa81f5906" :knowledge-point/title "Evaluating Flux Through a Surface"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "355bef10-0b8c-5536-a445-f01d12172fb8" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "3" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186275953} {:answer/id #uuid "59ce5885-1e3d-5f19-ba38-dbb31ab5b6a0" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-4" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186276282} {:answer/id #uuid "638c8aa6-4abb-5caf-80fe-7e02a183ce5f" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{5}{4}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186276379} {:answer/id #uuid "821420d2-3a8a-52ab-bf19-2fe3c2fc1b2d" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-\\frac{3}{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186276652} {:answer/id #uuid "c99962ef-c495-5547-948d-fcb7faccda71" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{1}{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186277268}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "c99962ef-c495-5547-948d-fcb7faccda71" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{1}{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186277268} :answer-field/id #uuid "c470c898-ccdc-5a03-914c-a796d495fee6" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186278070}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045486 :db/ident :question.difficulty/hard} :question/id #uuid "5f5f7b83-0f5c-511f-9e98-a4ae85732cc3" :question/math-academy-id "q-161278" :question/problem "Evaluate the surface integral\n\n$$\n{∬}_{S}⟨-x-z,\\,x-y,\\,-z⟩\\cdot \\text{d}S\n$$\n\nwhere the parametric surface $S$ is defined by the equations\n\n$$\nr(u,v)=⟨u+v,\\,v-u,\\,-v⟩\n$$\n\nfor $-1\\le u\\le 0$ and $0\\le v\\le 1.$" :question/worked-solution "For a surface $S$ with parametrization $r(u,v)$ for $(u,v)\\in D,$ the flux of a vector field $F$ over $S$ is given by\n\n$$\n{∬}_{S}F\\cdot \\text{d}S={∬}_{S}F\\cdot n\\,\\text{d}S={∬}_{D}F(r(u,v))\\cdot ({r}_{u}^{′}\\times {r}_{v}^{′})\\,\\text{d}A.\n$$\n\nWe first compute the tangent vectors to the grid curves:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{r}_{u}^{′} & =⟨\\frac{∂x}{∂u},\\,\\frac{∂y}{∂u},\\,\\frac{∂z}{∂u}⟩ \\\\  & =⟨\\frac{∂}{∂u}(u+v),\\,\\frac{∂}{∂u}(v-u),\\,\\frac{∂}{∂u}(-v)⟩ \\\\  & =⟨1,\\,-1,\\,0⟩ \\\\ {r}_{v}^{′} & =⟨\\frac{∂x}{∂v},\\,\\frac{∂y}{∂v},\\,\\frac{∂z}{∂v}⟩ \\\\  & =⟨\\frac{∂}{∂v}(u+v),\\,\\frac{∂}{∂v}(v-u),\\,\\frac{∂}{∂v}(-v)⟩ \\\\  & =⟨1,\\,1,\\,-1⟩\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, the fundamental vector product is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{r}_{u}^{′}\\times {r}_{v}^{′} & =|\\begin{aligned}i & j & k \\\\ 1 & -1 & 0 \\\\ 1 & 1 & -1\\end{aligned}| \\\\  & =⟨|\\begin{aligned}-1 & 0 \\\\ 1 & -1\\end{aligned}|,-|\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 \\\\ 1 & -1\\end{aligned}|,|\\begin{aligned}1 & -1 \\\\ 1 & 1\\end{aligned}|⟩ \\\\  & =⟨1,\\,1,\\,2⟩.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNext, we substitute the coordinate expressions of $r(u,v)$ into $F(x,y,z):$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}F(r(u,v)) & ={⟨-x-z,\\,x-y,\\,-z⟩|}_{x=u+v\\,y=v-u\\,z=-v} \\\\  & =⟨-(u+v)-(-v),\\,u+v-(v-u),\\,-(-v)⟩ \\\\  & =⟨-u,\\,2u,\\,v⟩\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, we calculate the dot product of $F$ and ${r}_{u}^{′}\\times {r}_{v}^{′}:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}F(r(u,v))\\cdot ({r}_{u}^{′}\\times {r}_{v}^{′}) & =⟨-u,\\,2u,\\,v⟩\\cdot ⟨1,\\,1,\\,2⟩ \\\\  & =(-u)\\cdot 1+2u\\cdot 1+v\\cdot 2 \\\\  & =-u+2u+2v \\\\  & =u+2v\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the surface integral evaluates to\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{∬}_{S}⟨-x-z,\\,x-y,\\,-z⟩\\cdot \\text{d}S & ={∬}_{D}F(r(u,v))\\cdot ({r}_{u}^{′}\\times {r}_{v}^{′})\\,\\text{d}A \\\\  & ={∬}_{D}(u+2v)\\,\\text{d}A \\\\  & ={\\int }_{-1}^{0}{\\int }_{0}^{1}(u+2v)\\,\\text{d}v\\,\\text{d}u \\\\  & ={\\int }_{-1}^{0}[uv+{v}^{2}]_{v=0}^{v=1}\\,\\text{d}u \\\\  & ={\\int }_{-1}^{0}(u+1)\\text{d}u \\\\  & ={[\\frac{1}{2}{u}^{2}+u]}_{-1}^{0} \\\\  & =-\\frac{1}{2}+1 \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{2}.\\end{aligned}\n$$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186278461 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "f322cca7-7530-50bf-b262-89faa81f5906" :knowledge-point/title "Evaluating Flux Through a Surface"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "0294c002-bd57-57d3-80b3-7fabcd4c0abb" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "3" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186275500} {:answer/id #uuid "0a1b7943-d74f-593a-a73d-4f7b2984e272" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-4" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186275563} {:answer/id #uuid "1db67973-261d-5c72-9a22-797cdd70f57d" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186275749} {:answer/id #uuid "6f3d9f2b-1400-51de-a847-0f9dbed86615" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{5}{4}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186276476} {:answer/id #uuid "8a4f51d4-c721-5278-ac9c-1a3d3fac3e2d" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-\\frac{3}{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186276726}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "1db67973-261d-5c72-9a22-797cdd70f57d" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186275749} :answer-field/id #uuid "1a7c1739-5bdb-5824-990f-022e95db8fc5" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186277772}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045486 :db/ident :question.difficulty/hard} :question/id #uuid "d4391484-a70c-5d5d-8147-34baf59f21fd" :question/math-academy-id "q-161283" :question/problem "Evaluate the surface integral\n\n$$\n{∬}_{S}⟨z,\\,2,\\,-3xy⟩\\cdot \\text{d}S\n$$\n\nwhere the parametric surface $S$ is defined by the equations\n\n$$\nr(u,v)=⟨u{v}^{2},\\,-1,\\,1-2u⟩\n$$\n\nfor $0\\le u\\le 1$ and $0\\le v\\le 1.$" :question/worked-solution "For a surface $S$ with parametrization $r(u,v)$ for $(u,v)\\in D,$ the flux of a vector field $F$ over $S$ is given by\n\n$$\n{∬}_{S}F\\cdot \\text{d}S={∬}_{S}F\\cdot n\\,\\text{d}S={∬}_{D}F(r(u,v))\\cdot ({r}_{u}^{′}\\times {r}_{v}^{′})\\,\\text{d}A.\n$$\n\nWe first compute the tangent vectors to the grid curves:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{r}_{u}^{′} & =⟨\\frac{∂x}{∂u},\\,\\frac{∂y}{∂u},\\,\\frac{∂z}{∂u}⟩ \\\\  & =⟨\\frac{∂}{∂u}(u{v}^{2}),\\,\\frac{∂}{∂u}(-1),\\,\\frac{∂}{∂u}(1-2u)⟩ \\\\  & =⟨{v}^{2},\\,0,\\,-2⟩ \\\\ {r}_{v}^{′} & =⟨\\frac{∂x}{∂v},\\,\\frac{∂y}{∂v},\\,\\frac{∂z}{∂v}⟩ \\\\  & =⟨\\frac{∂}{∂v}(u{v}^{2}),\\,\\frac{∂}{∂v}(-1),\\,\\frac{∂}{∂v}(1-2u)⟩ \\\\  & =⟨2uv,\\,0,\\,0⟩\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, the fundamental vector product is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{r}_{u}^{′}\\times {r}_{v}^{′} & =|\\begin{aligned}i & j & k \\\\ {v}^{2} & 0 & -2 \\\\ 2uv & 0 & 0\\end{aligned}| \\\\  & =⟨|\\begin{aligned}0 & -2 \\\\ 0 & 0\\end{aligned}|,-|\\begin{aligned}{v}^{2} & -2 \\\\ 2uv & 0\\end{aligned}|,|\\begin{aligned}{v}^{2} & 0 \\\\ 2uv & 0\\end{aligned}|⟩ \\\\  & =⟨0,\\,-4uv,\\,0⟩.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNext, we substitute the coordinate expressions of $r(u,v)$ into $F(x,y,z):$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}F(r(u,v)) & ={⟨z,\\,2,\\,-3xy⟩|}_{x=u{v}^{2}\\,y=-1\\,z=1-2u} \\\\  & =⟨1-2u,\\,2,\\,-3(u{v}^{2})(-1)⟩ \\\\  & =⟨1-2u,\\,2,\\,3u{v}^{2}⟩\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, we calculate the dot product of $F$ and ${r}_{u}^{′}\\times {r}_{v}^{′}:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}F(r(u,v))\\cdot ({r}_{u}^{′}\\times {r}_{v}^{′}) & =⟨1-2u,\\,2,\\,3u{v}^{2}⟩\\cdot ⟨0,\\,-4uv,\\,0⟩ \\\\  & =(1-2u)\\cdot 0+2\\cdot (-4uv)+3u{v}^{2}\\cdot 0 \\\\  & =-8uv\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the surface integral evaluates to\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{∬}_{S}⟨z,\\,2,\\,-3xy⟩\\cdot \\text{d}S & ={∬}_{D}F(r(u,v))\\cdot ({r}_{u}^{′}\\times {r}_{v}^{′})\\,\\text{d}A \\\\  & ={∬}_{D}(-8uv)\\,\\text{d}A \\\\  & =-8{\\int }_{0}^{1}{\\int }_{0}^{1}uv\\,\\text{d}v\\,\\text{d}u \\\\  & =-8{\\int }_{0}^{1}u\\,\\text{d}u{\\int }_{0}^{1}v\\,\\text{d}v\\, \\\\  & =-8\\cdot {[\\frac{1}{2}{u}^{2}]}_{0}^{1}\\cdot {[\\frac{1}{2}{v}^{2}]}_{0}^{1} \\\\  & =-8(\\frac{1}{2})(\\frac{1}{2}) \\\\  & =-2.\\end{aligned}\n$$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186421784 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "f322cca7-7530-50bf-b262-89faa81f5906" :knowledge-point/title "Evaluating Flux Through a Surface"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "3a219dca-1e12-574f-9fc3-d709a89775ad" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "3" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186421769} {:answer/id #uuid "4b502ee2-042d-5a3e-86ae-ba6ad14e00b2" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-\\frac{23}{4}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186421770} {:answer/id #uuid "5be10e6b-2fc0-5157-8d4c-a6365644fb4a" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{17}{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186421771} {:answer/id #uuid "ac272ec2-a123-566b-9ae4-94a591001c16" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-5" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186421776} {:answer/id #uuid "bb4a967e-d128-5262-a38b-86976eb912e7" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-\\frac{22}{3}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186421777}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "4b502ee2-042d-5a3e-86ae-ba6ad14e00b2" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-\\frac{23}{4}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186421770} :answer-field/id #uuid "de26f158-7713-5413-99c7-ec6ea96881bb" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186421782}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "4c963e37-fb2b-5cec-bc6e-5cbde0fb10aa" :question/math-academy-id "q-161258" :question/problem "Evaluate the surface integral\n\n$$\n{∬}_{S}⟨3x,\\,-{y}^{2},\\,2⟩\\cdot \\text{d}S\n$$\n\nwhere the parametric surface $S$ is defined by\n\n$$\nr(u,v)=⟨3uv,\\,u,\\,-v⟩\n$$\n\nover the domain $D={(u,v)\\,:\\,0\\le u\\le 1,\\,0\\le v\\le 1}.$\n\n*Hint: You can use the fact that ${r}_{u}^{′}\\times {r}_{v}^{′}=⟨-1,\\,3v,\\,-3u⟩.$*" :question/worked-solution "For a surface $S$ with parametrization $r(u,v)$ for $(u,v)\\in D,$ the flux of a vector field $F$ over $S$ is given by\n\n$$\n{∬}_{S}F\\cdot \\text{d}S={∬}_{S}F\\cdot n\\,\\text{d}S={∬}_{D}F(r(u,v))\\cdot ({r}_{u}^{′}\\times {r}_{v}^{′})\\,\\text{d}A.\n$$\n\nWe're given that the fundamental vector product for our surface is\n\n$$\n{r}_{u}^{′}\\times {r}_{v}^{′}=⟨-1,\\,3v,\\,-3u⟩.\n$$\n\nNext, we substitute the coordinate expressions of $r(u,v)$ into $F(x,y,z):$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}F(r(u,v)) & ={⟨3x,\\,-{y}^{2},\\,2⟩|}_{x=3uv\\,y=u\\,z=-v} \\\\  & =⟨3(3uv),\\,-{u}^{2},\\,2⟩ \\\\  & =⟨9uv,\\,-{u}^{2},\\,2⟩\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThen, we calculate the dot product of $F$ and ${r}_{u}^{′}\\times {r}_{v}^{′}:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}F(r(u,v))\\cdot ({r}_{u}^{′}\\times {r}_{v}^{′}) & =⟨9uv,\\,-{u}^{2},\\,2⟩\\cdot ⟨-1,\\,3v,\\,-3u⟩ \\\\  & =9uv\\cdot (-1)+(-{u}^{2})\\cdot 3v+2\\cdot (-3u) \\\\  & =-9uv-3{u}^{2}v-6u\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the surface integral evaluates to\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{∬}_{S}⟨3x,\\,-{y}^{2},\\,2⟩\\cdot \\text{d}S & ={∬}_{D}F(r(u,v))\\cdot ({r}_{u}^{′}\\times {r}_{v}^{′})\\,\\text{d}A \\\\  & ={∬}_{D}(-9uv-3{u}^{2}v-6u)\\,\\text{d}A \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{1}{\\int }_{0}^{1}(-9uv-3{u}^{2}v-6u)\\,\\text{d}u\\,\\text{d}v \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{1}{[-\\frac{9}{2}{u}^{2}v-{u}^{3}v-3{u}^{2}]}_{u=0}^{u=1}\\,\\text{d}v \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{1}(-\\frac{11}{2}v-3)\\text{d}v \\\\  & ={[-\\frac{11}{4}{v}^{2}-3v]}_{0}^{1} \\\\  & =-\\frac{11}{4}-3 \\\\  & =-\\frac{23}{4}.\\end{aligned}\n$$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186421785 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "f322cca7-7530-50bf-b262-89faa81f5906" :knowledge-point/title "Evaluating Flux Through a Surface"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "127c5717-261e-5aef-838e-be5fab62b6d9" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-\\frac{3}{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186421765} {:answer/id #uuid "176992fe-e63a-5f75-8661-ee649edc6971" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{1}{3}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186421766} {:answer/id #uuid "794b5eb2-d0f5-57bd-8363-4337b7e59452" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-\\frac{1}{3}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186421772} {:answer/id #uuid "cb9f4e2e-e860-55d7-8d5c-c33be0190db3" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-\\frac{1}{4}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186421778} {:answer/id #uuid "d7fec48c-2c4b-5a3b-8559-e99202ca21e4" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-\\frac{1}{8}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186421779}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "127c5717-261e-5aef-838e-be5fab62b6d9" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-\\frac{3}{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186421765} :answer-field/id #uuid "b8009739-528a-5b9d-8b7a-977eb7894c6b" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186421781}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "f3288098-3c26-556d-b6c9-f206da47adfb" :question/math-academy-id "q-162593" :question/problem "Evaluate the surface integral\n\n$$\n{∬}_{S}⟨3z,\\,-2x,\\,-y⟩\\cdot \\text{d}S\n$$\n\nwhere the parametric surface $S$ is defined by the equations\n\n$$\nr(u,v)=⟨-v,\\,-u,\\,{u}^{2}⟩\n$$\n\nfor $0\\le u\\le 1$ and $0\\le v\\le 1.$" :question/worked-solution "For a surface $S$ with parametrization $r(u,v)$ for $(u,v)\\in D,$ the flux of a vector field $F$ over $S$ is given by\n\n$$\n{∬}_{S}F\\cdot \\text{d}S={∬}_{S}F\\cdot n\\,\\text{d}S={∬}_{D}F(r(u,v))\\cdot ({r}_{u}^{′}\\times {r}_{v}^{′})\\,\\text{d}A.\n$$\n\nWe first compute the tangent vectors to the grid curves:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{r}_{u}^{′} & =⟨\\frac{∂x}{∂u},\\,\\frac{∂y}{∂u},\\,\\frac{∂z}{∂u}⟩ \\\\  & =⟨\\frac{∂}{∂u}(-v),\\,\\frac{∂}{∂u}(-u),\\,\\frac{∂}{∂u}({u}^{2})⟩ \\\\  & =⟨0,\\,-1,\\,2u⟩ \\\\ {r}_{v}^{′} & =⟨\\frac{∂x}{∂v},\\,\\frac{∂y}{∂v},\\,\\frac{∂z}{∂v}⟩ \\\\  & =⟨\\frac{∂}{∂v}(-v),\\,\\frac{∂}{∂v}(-u),\\,\\frac{∂}{∂v}({u}^{2})⟩ \\\\  & =⟨-1,\\,0,\\,0⟩\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, the fundamental vector product is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{r}_{u}^{′}\\times {r}_{v}^{′} & =|\\begin{aligned}i & j & k \\\\ 0 & -1 & 2u \\\\ -1 & 0 & 0\\end{aligned}| \\\\  & =⟨|\\begin{aligned}-1 & 2u \\\\ 0 & 0\\end{aligned}|,-|\\begin{aligned}0 & 2u \\\\ -1 & 0\\end{aligned}|,|\\begin{aligned}0 & -1 \\\\ -1 & 0\\end{aligned}|⟩ \\\\  & =⟨0,\\,-2u,\\,-1⟩.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNext, we substitute the coordinate expressions of $r(u,v)$ into $F(x,y,z):$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}F(r(u,v)) & ={⟨3z,\\,-2x,\\,-y⟩|}_{x=-v\\,y=-u\\,z={u}^{2}} \\\\  & =⟨3{u}^{2},\\,-2(-v),\\,-(-u)⟩ \\\\  & =⟨3{u}^{2},\\,2v,\\,u⟩\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThen, we calculate the dot product of $F$ and ${r}_{u}^{′}\\times {r}_{v}^{′}:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}F(r(u,v))\\cdot ({r}_{u}^{′}\\times {r}_{v}^{′}) & =⟨3{u}^{2},\\,2v,\\,u⟩\\cdot ⟨0,\\,-2u,\\,-1⟩ \\\\  & =3{u}^{2}\\cdot 0+2v\\cdot (-2u)+u\\cdot (-1) \\\\  & =-4uv-u\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the surface integral evaluates to\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{∬}_{S}⟨3z,\\,-2x,\\,-y⟩\\cdot \\text{d}S & ={∬}_{D}F(r(u,v))\\cdot ({r}_{u}^{′}\\times {r}_{v}^{′})\\,\\text{d}A \\\\  & ={∬}_{D}(-4uv-u)\\,\\text{d}A \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{1}{\\int }_{0}^{1}(-4uv-u)\\,\\text{d}u\\,\\text{d}v \\\\  & =-{\\int }_{0}^{1}{\\int }_{0}^{1}(4uv+u)\\,\\text{d}u\\,\\text{d}v \\\\  & =-{\\int }_{0}^{1}{[2{u}^{2}v+\\frac{1}{2}{u}^{2}]}_{u=0}^{u=1}\\,\\text{d}v \\\\  & =-{\\int }_{0}^{1}(2v+\\frac{1}{2})\\text{d}v \\\\  & =-{[{v}^{2}+\\frac{1}{2}v]}_{0}^{1} \\\\  & =-\\frac{3}{2}.\\end{aligned}\n$$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186434831 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "f322cca7-7530-50bf-b262-89faa81f5906" :knowledge-point/title "Evaluating Flux Through a Surface"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "1c4ed277-51d3-5190-9f15-e73dd884cf47" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "6" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186434819} {:answer/id #uuid "471dabbc-d133-52dc-b559-394801c709a2" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{7}{3}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186434821} {:answer/id #uuid "777af6b2-9aef-5099-aac7-98b1ec37120e" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{5}{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186434822} {:answer/id #uuid "8a1f231c-84b6-5409-b4c5-4c9196b18b4b" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "3" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186434823} {:answer/id #uuid "de47629f-21da-52b1-941b-ae2f3625cecc" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186434827}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "1c4ed277-51d3-5190-9f15-e73dd884cf47" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "6" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186434819} :answer-field/id #uuid "5a1a0c12-6b57-5589-b4e1-416cdc457a68" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186434828}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "f5815497-10bb-5d31-b1ef-c78b6eb79a17" :question/math-academy-id "q-161259" :question/problem "Evaluate the surface integral\n\n$$\n{∬}_{S}⟨x,\\,y,\\,-z⟩\\cdot \\text{d}S\n$$\n\nwhere the parametric surface $S$ is defined by\n\n$$\nr(u,v)=⟨u+v,\\,v-u,\\,uv⟩\n$$\n\nover the domain $D=\\{(u,v)\\,:\\,-2\\le u\\le 0,\\,0\\le v\\le 1\\}.$\n\n*Hint: You can use the fact that ${r}_{u}^{′}\\times {r}_{v}^{′}=⟨-u-v,\\,v-u,\\,2⟩.$*" :question/worked-solution "For a surface $S$ with parametrization $r(u,v)$ for $(u,v)\\in D,$ the flux of a vector field $F$ over $S$ is given by\n\n$$\n{∬}_{S}F\\cdot \\text{d}S={∬}_{S}F\\cdot n\\,\\text{d}S={∬}_{D}F(r(u,v))\\cdot ({r}_{u}^{′}\\times {r}_{v}^{′})\\,\\text{d}A.\n$$\n\nWe're given that the fundamental vector product for our surface is\n\n$$\n{r}_{u}^{′}\\times {r}_{v}^{′}=⟨-u-v,\\,v-u,\\,2⟩.\n$$\n\nNext, we substitute the coordinate expressions of $r(u,v)$ into $F(x,y,z):$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}F(r(u,v)) & ={⟨x,\\,y,\\,-z⟩|}_{x=u+v\\,y=v-u\\,z=uv} \\\\  & =⟨u+v,\\,v-u,\\,-uv⟩\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThen, we calculate the dot product of $F$ and ${r}_{u}^{′}\\times {r}_{v}^{′}:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}F(r(u,v))\\cdot ({r}_{u}^{′}\\times {r}_{v}^{′}) & =⟨u+v,\\,v-u,\\,-uv⟩\\cdot ⟨-u-v,\\,v-u,\\,2⟩ \\\\  & =(u+v)\\cdot (-u-v)+(v-u)\\cdot (v-u)+(-uv)\\cdot 2 \\\\  & =-{u}^{2}-2uv-{v}^{2}+{v}^{2}-2uv+{u}^{2}-2uv \\\\  & =-6uv\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the surface integral evaluates to\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{∬}_{S}⟨x,\\,y,\\,-z⟩\\cdot \\text{d}S & ={∬}_{D}F(r(u,v))\\cdot ({r}_{u}^{′}\\times {r}_{v}^{′})\\,\\text{d}A \\\\  & ={∬}_{D}(-6uv)\\,\\text{d}A \\\\  & =-6{\\int }_{0}^{1}{\\int }_{-2}^{0}uv\\,\\text{d}u\\,\\text{d}v \\\\  & =-6{\\int }_{0}^{1}v\\,\\text{d}v{\\int }_{-2}^{0}u\\,\\text{d}u \\\\  & =-6\\cdot [\\frac{1}{2}{v}^{2}]_{0}^{1}\\cdot {[\\frac{1}{2}{u}^{2}]}_{-2}^{0} \\\\  & =-6\\cdot \\frac{1}{2}\\cdot (-2) \\\\  & =6.\\end{aligned}\n$$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186531811 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "f322cca7-7530-50bf-b262-89faa81f5906" :knowledge-point/title "Evaluating Flux Through a Surface"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "0ed89854-ce24-5e33-9d9f-77633ee05901" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "576" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186531805} {:answer/id #uuid "5435d236-631f-5cf6-a1af-7c24ebc30e43" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-128" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186531816} {:answer/id #uuid "585b87b5-9e11-5026-936e-4e61825b1445" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-224" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186531817} {:answer/id #uuid "be0db405-a911-5d94-9f80-93c89ee42be1" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "48" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186531830} {:answer/id #uuid "c970e40f-e018-5931-8bb7-7afdd50e22cf" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "224" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186531831}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "c970e40f-e018-5931-8bb7-7afdd50e22cf" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "224" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186531831} :answer-field/id #uuid "a843646c-3bd8-57f7-b6c7-b5130883f76b" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186531825}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "2a372134-3f0d-5612-aa85-09775257279c" :question/problem "Evaluate the surface integral\n\n$$\n{∬}_{S}⟨z,\\,x,\\,y⟩\\cdot \\text{d}S\n$$\n\nwhere the parametric surface $S$ is defined by\n\n$$\nr(u,v)=⟨2 u + v + 1,\\,u + v,\\,u - v⟩\n$$\n\nover the domain $D={(u,v)\\,:\\,-1\\le u\\le 3,\\,-1\\le v\\le 3}.$\n\n*Hint: You can use the fact that ${r}_{u}^{′}\\times {r}_{v}^{′}=⟨-2,\\,3,\\,1⟩.$*" :question/worked-solution "For a surface $S$ with parametrization $r(u,v)$ for $(u,v)\\in D,$ the flux of a vector field $F$ over $S$ is given by\n\n$$\n{∬}_{S}F\\cdot \\text{d}S={∬}_{S}F\\cdot n\\,\\text{d}S={∬}_{D}F(r(u,v))\\cdot ({r}_{u}^{′}\\times {r}_{v}^{′})\\,\\text{d}A.\n$$\n\nWe're given that the fundamental vector product for our surface is\n\n$$\n{r}_{u}^{′}\\times {r}_{v}^{′}=⟨-2,\\,3,\\,1⟩.\n$$\n\nNext, we substitute the coordinate expressions of $r(u,v)$ into $F(x,y,z):$\n\n$$\nF(r(u,v))=⟨u - v,\\,2 u + v + 1,\\,u + v⟩\n$$\n\nThen, we calculate the dot product of $F$ and ${r}_{u}^{′}\\times {r}_{v}^{′}:$\n\n$$\n⟨u - v,\\,2 u + v + 1,\\,u + v⟩\\cdot ⟨-2,\\,3,\\,1⟩=5 u + 6 v + 3\n$$\n\nTherefore, the surface integral evaluates to\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{∬}_{S}F\\cdot \\text{d}S & ={\\int }_{-1}^{3}{\\int }_{-1}^{3}(5 u + 6 v + 3)\\,\\text{d}v\\,\\text{d}u \\\\ & ={\\int }_{-1}^{3}[v \\left(5 u + 3 v + 3\\right)]_{v=-1}^{v=3}\\,\\text{d}u \\\\ & ={\\int }_{-1}^{3}(20 u + 36)\\,\\text{d}u \\\\ & =[2 u \\left(5 u + 18\\right)]_{-1}^{3} \\\\ & =224.\\end{aligned}\n$$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186531812 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "f322cca7-7530-50bf-b262-89faa81f5906" :knowledge-point/title "Evaluating Flux Through a Surface"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "04d3bf91-1b9e-50e1-b487-002e4121a6ed" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "78" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186531804} {:answer/id #uuid "42225fe9-ade9-5b18-9132-55f036dc3f8d" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-78" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186531813} {:answer/id #uuid "b4be5f22-1fbe-5fac-ba0f-a34045b52bed" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "1092" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186531828} {:answer/id #uuid "b9ba4c1a-4db7-52c0-a20a-62aa2d4a4381" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "120" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186531829} {:answer/id #uuid "f13f373d-207a-56fa-99a9-a1ac19de5e8e" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "23" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186531836}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "04d3bf91-1b9e-50e1-b487-002e4121a6ed" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "78" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186531804} :answer-field/id #uuid "7f9f5640-40e0-5f7c-a1ff-41e54d4e16f6" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186531819}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "326926db-5725-5b57-8003-30f866bb2f70" :question/problem "Evaluate the surface integral\n\n$$\n{∬}_{S}⟨z,\\,x,\\,y⟩\\cdot \\text{d}S\n$$\n\nwhere the parametric surface $S$ is defined by\n\n$$\nr(u,v)=⟨2 u + v + 1,\\,u + v,\\,u - v⟩\n$$\n\nover the domain $D={(u,v)\\,:\\,-2\\le u\\le 1,\\,-1\\le v\\le 3}.$\n\n*Hint: You can use the fact that ${r}_{u}^{′}\\times {r}_{v}^{′}=⟨-2,\\,3,\\,1⟩.$*" :question/worked-solution "For a surface $S$ with parametrization $r(u,v)$ for $(u,v)\\in D,$ the flux of a vector field $F$ over $S$ is given by\n\n$$\n{∬}_{S}F\\cdot \\text{d}S={∬}_{S}F\\cdot n\\,\\text{d}S={∬}_{D}F(r(u,v))\\cdot ({r}_{u}^{′}\\times {r}_{v}^{′})\\,\\text{d}A.\n$$\n\nWe're given that the fundamental vector product for our surface is\n\n$$\n{r}_{u}^{′}\\times {r}_{v}^{′}=⟨-2,\\,3,\\,1⟩.\n$$\n\nNext, we substitute the coordinate expressions of $r(u,v)$ into $F(x,y,z):$\n\n$$\nF(r(u,v))=⟨u - v,\\,2 u + v + 1,\\,u + v⟩\n$$\n\nThen, we calculate the dot product of $F$ and ${r}_{u}^{′}\\times {r}_{v}^{′}:$\n\n$$\n⟨u - v,\\,2 u + v + 1,\\,u + v⟩\\cdot ⟨-2,\\,3,\\,1⟩=5 u + 6 v + 3\n$$\n\nTherefore, the surface integral evaluates to\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{∬}_{S}F\\cdot \\text{d}S & ={\\int }_{-2}^{1}{\\int }_{-1}^{3}(5 u + 6 v + 3)\\,\\text{d}v\\,\\text{d}u \\\\ & ={\\int }_{-2}^{1}[v \\left(5 u + 3 v + 3\\right)]_{v=-1}^{v=3}\\,\\text{d}u \\\\ & ={\\int }_{-2}^{1}(20 u + 36)\\,\\text{d}u \\\\ & =[2 u \\left(5 u + 18\\right)]_{-2}^{1} \\\\ & =78.\\end{aligned}\n$$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186531818 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "f322cca7-7530-50bf-b262-89faa81f5906" :knowledge-point/title "Evaluating Flux Through a Surface"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "01cb0663-140c-55be-a037-3632d1f8ad3a" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-128" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186531802} {:answer/id #uuid "21032641-051e-5d4d-80d1-e40cdd7891b2" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "128" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186531809} {:answer/id #uuid "51c051c6-3526-5041-b89e-19c85bcb555e" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "1792" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186531815} {:answer/id #uuid "dc46265a-5d8a-51ce-82ba-a5675e274c8e" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "232" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186531834} {:answer/id #uuid "e1628a2d-7339-59ec-a5d5-b85e611c7df6" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{122}{3}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186531835}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "21032641-051e-5d4d-80d1-e40cdd7891b2" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "128" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186531809} :answer-field/id #uuid "88ff5813-50ae-5cf5-8858-de04c9c1b633" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186531822}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "6ee8b4d4-16bf-53a3-a6a2-18b752c2a7e0" :question/problem "Evaluate the surface integral\n\n$$\n{∬}_{S}⟨z,\\,x,\\,y⟩\\cdot \\text{d}S\n$$\n\nwhere the parametric surface $S$ is defined by\n\n$$\nr(u,v)=⟨2 u + v + 1,\\,u + v,\\,u - v⟩\n$$\n\nover the domain $D={(u,v)\\,:\\,-3\\le u\\le 1,\\,2\\le v\\le 4}.$\n\n*Hint: You can use the fact that ${r}_{u}^{′}\\times {r}_{v}^{′}=⟨-2,\\,3,\\,1⟩.$*" :question/worked-solution "For a surface $S$ with parametrization $r(u,v)$ for $(u,v)\\in D,$ the flux of a vector field $F$ over $S$ is given by\n\n$$\n{∬}_{S}F\\cdot \\text{d}S={∬}_{S}F\\cdot n\\,\\text{d}S={∬}_{D}F(r(u,v))\\cdot ({r}_{u}^{′}\\times {r}_{v}^{′})\\,\\text{d}A.\n$$\n\nWe're given that the fundamental vector product for our surface is\n\n$$\n{r}_{u}^{′}\\times {r}_{v}^{′}=⟨-2,\\,3,\\,1⟩.\n$$\n\nNext, we substitute the coordinate expressions of $r(u,v)$ into $F(x,y,z):$\n\n$$\nF(r(u,v))=⟨u - v,\\,2 u + v + 1,\\,u + v⟩\n$$\n\nThen, we calculate the dot product of $F$ and ${r}_{u}^{′}\\times {r}_{v}^{′}:$\n\n$$\n⟨u - v,\\,2 u + v + 1,\\,u + v⟩\\cdot ⟨-2,\\,3,\\,1⟩=5 u + 6 v + 3\n$$\n\nTherefore, the surface integral evaluates to\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{∬}_{S}F\\cdot \\text{d}S & ={\\int }_{-3}^{1}{\\int }_{2}^{4}(5 u + 6 v + 3)\\,\\text{d}v\\,\\text{d}u \\\\ & ={\\int }_{-3}^{1}[v \\left(5 u + 3 v + 3\\right)]_{v=2}^{v=4}\\,\\text{d}u \\\\ & ={\\int }_{-3}^{1}(10 u + 42)\\,\\text{d}u \\\\ & =[u \\left(5 u + 42\\right)]_{-3}^{1} \\\\ & =128.\\end{aligned}\n$$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186531826 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "f322cca7-7530-50bf-b262-89faa81f5906" :knowledge-point/title "Evaluating Flux Through a Surface"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "1e271977-32a1-57a7-a474-394248fe0e9a" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "144" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186531808} {:answer/id #