Then, we calculate the dot product of $F$ and ${r}_{u}^{′}\\times {r}_{v}^{′}:$\n\n$$\n⟨u - v,\\,2 u + v + 1,\\,u + v⟩\\cdot ⟨-2,\\,3,\\,1⟩=5 u + 6 v + 3\n$$\n\nTherefore, the surface integral evaluates to\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{∬}_{S}F\\cdot \\text{d}S & ={\\int }_{2}^{4}{\\int }_{2}^{4}(5 u + 6 v + 3)\\,\\text{d}v\\,\\text{d}u \\\\ & ={\\int }_{2}^{4}[v \\left(5 u + 3 v + 3\\right)]_{v=2}^{v=4}\\,\\text{d}u \\\\ & ={\\int }_{2}^{4}(10 u + 42)\\,\\text{d}u \\\\ & =[u \\left(5 u + 42\\right)]_{2}^{4} \\\\ & =144.\\end{aligned}\n$$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186531827 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "f322cca7-7530-50bf-b262-89faa81f5906" :knowledge-point/title "Evaluating Flux Through a Surface"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "04a7f69c-4b83-50f9-933c-1fa3c60a2e76" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "- \\frac{27}{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186531803} {:answer/id #uuid "1b6bb199-c4f1-5942-aa25-3201086ffc65" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "- \\frac{9}{4}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186531807} {:answer/id #uuid "4bde3cba-d7a2-5b3d-bcfc-510fcdbe781e" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "45" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186531814} {:answer/id #uuid "ca8d0cf4-25d1-56ab-94d5-7f2008bec7af" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-18" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186531832} {:answer/id #uuid "d97e42ef-dfa1-5464-a6f5-bdc6b4e0564d" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{27}{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186531833}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "d97e42ef-dfa1-5464-a6f5-bdc6b4e0564d" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{27}{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186531833} :answer-field/id #uuid "0f73a17e-5f4d-5c48-88d9-7569eef6e206" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186531806}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "b4051a5d-c9b9-518f-92fa-031fa84284a7" :question/problem "Evaluate the surface integral\n\n$$\n{∬}_{S}⟨z,\\,x,\\,y⟩\\cdot \\text{d}S\n$$\n\nwhere the parametric surface $S$ is defined by\n\n$$\nr(u,v)=⟨2 u + v + 1,\\,u + v,\\,u - v⟩\n$$\n\nover the domain $D={(u,v)\\,:\\,-3\\le u\\le 0,\\,1\\le v\\le 2}.$\n\n*Hint: You can use the fact that ${r}_{u}^{′}\\times {r}_{v}^{′}=⟨-2,\\,3,\\,1⟩.$*" :question/worked-solution "For a surface $S$ with parametrization $r(u,v)$ for $(u,v)\\in D,$ the flux of a vector field $F$ over $S$ is given by\n\n$$\n{∬}_{S}F\\cdot \\text{d}S={∬}_{S}F\\cdot n\\,\\text{d}S={∬}_{D}F(r(u,v))\\cdot ({r}_{u}^{′}\\times {r}_{v}^{′})\\,\\text{d}A.\n$$\n\nWe're given that the fundamental vector product for our surface is\n\n$$\n{r}_{u}^{′}\\times {r}_{v}^{′}=⟨-2,\\,3,\\,1⟩.\n$$\n\nNext, we substitute the coordinate expressions of $r(u,v)$ into $F(x,y,z):$\n\n$$\nF(r(u,v))=⟨u - v,\\,2 u + v + 1,\\,u + v⟩\n$$\n\nThen, we calculate the dot product of $F$ and ${r}_{u}^{′}\\times {r}_{v}^{′}:$\n\n$$\n⟨u - v,\\,2 u + v + 1,\\,u + v⟩\\cdot ⟨-2,\\,3,\\,1⟩=5 u + 6 v + 3\n$$\n\nTherefore, the surface integral evaluates to\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{∬}_{S}F\\cdot \\text{d}S & ={\\int }_{-3}^{0}{\\int }_{1}^{2}(5 u + 6 v + 3)\\,\\text{d}v\\,\\text{d}u \\\\ & ={\\int }_{-3}^{0}[v \\left(5 u + 3 v + 3\\right)]_{v=1}^{v=2}\\,\\text{d}u \\\\ & ={\\int }_{-3}^{0}(5 u + 12)\\,\\text{d}u \\\\ & =[\\frac{u \\left(5 u + 24\\right)}{2}]_{-3}^{0} \\\\ & =\\frac{27}{2}.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] :knowledge-point/title "Evaluating Flux Through a Surface"}]}
